1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,340
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:36,100
[HANA] "Dear Yuru, I have your
fake sister and a village child.

3
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:39,140
On the next full moon
at the Hour of the Boar,

4
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:41,980
come to Fujimurayama
Warehouse One."

5
00:01:42,810 --> 00:01:44,190
[Yuru grunts]

6
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:48,900
[Yozakura growls]

7
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:52,280
[YURU] How? Where did this thing
come from?

8
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,910
Dera! Shoot this thing!

9
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:57,160
[all gasp]

10
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:04,750
[grunts]

11
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,460
[DERA] Yuru!

12
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:17,510
[Yuru grunts]

13
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,350
[IVAN] None of these people
had to die

14
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:21,100
if Yuru had come alone
like I told him.

15
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,940
And if you're not to blame,

16
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,110
whoever was the master
of those sword daemons

17
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,610
before you spilled their blood.

18
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:33,690
I can smell Mine and Nagisa
on those blades.

19
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:34,700
[Dera grunts]

20
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:36,780
[Ivan chuckles]

21
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:45,160
[RIGHT] Dera,
leave us and find Yuru.

22
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:48,420
We'll take this man
and his daemons alive.

23
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,210
[LEFT] A gift for our master.

24
00:02:54,130 --> 00:02:55,090
[Yuru gasps]

25
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,140
[Yozakura growls]

26
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:03,100
[both grunt]

27
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:06,270
-[Shingo gasps]
-What the...

28
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:07,440
♪

29
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,650
[YURU] Smoke signals.

30
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:12,900
[grunts]

31
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:15,900
Danji's asking us to help him.

32
00:03:15,990 --> 00:03:17,320
[Azami cries]

33
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:19,780
[ASA (FAKE)]
Azami, it'll be okay.

34
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:23,160
Someone's on their way
to save us right now.

35
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:24,290
Who is it?

36
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,620
My brother.

37
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:27,790
[both grunting]

38
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,750
-You really came!
-Yuru!

39
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:37,180
So I thought I'd find
my brother here.

40
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:42,260
[Asa (fake) and Azami trembling]

41
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:50,270
-It's Asa!
-Get her!

42
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:52,400
[growling]

43
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,860
[grunts]

44
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,570
[groaning]

45
00:03:57,650 --> 00:03:58,700
[both screaming]

46
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,700
[Embrace growls]

47
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:04,910
[FUYUKI] Thank you.

48
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,330
[gasps] So easily?

49
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:10,170
Isn't Asa supposed to be
weaker in the nighttime?

50
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,540
Wait, I thought so, too!

51
00:04:12,170 --> 00:04:15,420
So that means
Break is just that strong!

52
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,340
[both gasping]

53
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:19,510
-Yin and Yang...
-[both squeal]

54
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:20,930
...grab those two.

55
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,480
[both gasp]

56
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,900
[BOTH] Uh?

57
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:35,190
[both gasp]

58
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:37,070
-[both gasping]
-[ASA] Hey.

59
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:38,110
[both yelp]

60
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,200
[ASA (FAKE)]
What's going on here?

61
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:44,660
Any other hostages?
Or is it just her? Answer me.

62
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:48,040
Azami's the only village child
they took.

63
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,170
But she's got
nothing to do with this!

64
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:52,080
She's just
an innocent bystander!

65
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,170
If you want revenge,
leave her out.

66
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:55,340
[Asa grunts]

67
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:01,970
I've got a lot of things to say.
So much to say, but later.

68
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,260
For now,
just stay where you are.

69
00:05:05,350 --> 00:05:07,600
I'll let you out
when I'm done working.

70
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:10,190
And as soon as I do,

71
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:12,520
you will tell my brother
everything.

72
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,270
And I mean everything!
Leave nothing out!

73
00:05:18,150 --> 00:05:20,780
Hey, Yin and Yang?
You can let go of me now.

74
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:26,410
I beg you,
don't lie to Yuru anymore.

75
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:28,870
[both gasp softly]

76
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:31,580
♪

77
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,290
[Embrace growling]

78
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:38,590
[both gasping]

79
00:05:38,670 --> 00:05:40,590
[MAN 1] Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

80
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:42,930
[MAN 2] There's no way.

81
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:53,350
[both whimpering]

82
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:56,520
[laughs]

83
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,820
[men screaming]

84
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:01,820
[MAN 1] Who is this woman?
She took my daemons!

85
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:04,240
[MAN 2] I'm just a normal dude!
Spare me!

86
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,950
[both screaming]

87
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:07,030
[ALL] Uh?

88
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:09,660
So this is Oedo Transport.

89
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,580
Seems like Mamegarasu's intel
was right on the money.

90
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:14,870
[YURU] That's gotta be where
they're keeping the hostages.

91
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,580
It is so loud in there.

92
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:20,000
Mm-hmm. The real Asa's inside
tearing it apart.

93
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,050
Hmm? Uh?

94
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:23,930
[YURU] Huh.

95
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:27,510
[whimpers]

96
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,470
[cries]

97
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:32,230
Yuru, you came to save me.

98
00:06:32,310 --> 00:06:34,230
Huh? Don't be stupid.

99
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:36,440
Do you really think
I'd come all this way

100
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,730
to save some
whiny little punk like you?

101
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:40,860
Hey, get off of me.

102
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,530
Aw. I heard about
a couple people

103
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:44,320
wearing suits walking their dog.

104
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,070
Yeah, you've gotta be
those aliens

105
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,320
-Ken told me about.
-[Yuru continues indistinctly]

106
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:48,700
[FEMALE DAEMON] We're daemons.

107
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:50,040
[MALE DAEMON] Nice to meet you.

108
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:53,080
[DERA] Then over there,
that's gotta be Danji?

109
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:55,000
I've never seen
his true form before.

110
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,670
Right and Left
are busy somewhere,

111
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:59,210
pursuing a lead they found
on my mom and dad.

112
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:01,130
The only reason I'm here
is because I trust them

113
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:02,460
to take care of themselves.

114
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:04,010
-[Dera chuckles]
-This was a simple process

115
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:06,550
of elimination.
I didn't come to save you.

116
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:08,550
Why are you laughing, Dera?
Back off!

117
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,310
[ALL] Huh?

118
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:12,060
[MAN 1] Someone help! [screams]

119
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:14,520
But man...

120
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,600
If Asa's already got things
covered here, why'd I bother?

121
00:07:17,690 --> 00:07:20,230
[men groaning]

122
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:25,320
Do you think everyone's okay
at the manor?

123
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:28,070
They've got enough manpower.
I'm sure they're fine.

124
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:31,660
Damn. No one said
Break was gonna be here, too.

125
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:35,040
You shouldn't believe
everything you hear so easily.

126
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:37,420
I know it was all
part of the plan,

127
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:40,670
but acting like a broken record?
Not easy.

128
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:43,630
What? So you were acting?
Could have fooled me.

129
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:45,630
I want to see my brother.
I want to see my brother.

130
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:47,550
I want to see my brother.
I want to see my brother.

131
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:51,260
Of course that was acting.
Plus, Ai really hammed it up.

132
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:52,970
You think? It seemed to me

133
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:55,680
like she had your impression
down pat.

134
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:58,270
Someone had to inform me
when she took your place.

135
00:07:58,350 --> 00:07:59,560
I didn't have a clue at all.

136
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,150
[Asa gasps]

137
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:03,610
I hear my brother's voice!

138
00:08:03,690 --> 00:08:06,530
-[grunts]
-And now you're hearing things?

139
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:08,490
Oof, poor girl.

140
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,410
I knew I'd find you out here!

141
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:14,240
Uh? How the hell?

142
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:17,160
[ASA] Are you all right, Yuru?
You haven't died?

143
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:20,000
Who's got time to die?
I'm way too busy living!

144
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,250
[Asa chuckles]

145
00:08:21,330 --> 00:08:22,750
[FUYUKI] He really was there.

146
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,420
Did you find the village kid
they were holding hostage?

147
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,670
Plus there's Asa.
Well, the fake one.

148
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,220
Yep, no worries.

149
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,260
I put them both
somewhere they would be safe.

150
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:33,470
Praise me! And gimme a hug!

151
00:08:33,550 --> 00:08:35,430
Why don't you ask Right?
He's great at 'em.

152
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,310
[chuckles]

153
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:40,190
[FEMALE DAEMON] Your other half
and the kid are just fine.

154
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:42,020
[MALE DAEMON]
How about it, Danji?

155
00:08:42,110 --> 00:08:44,650
-That's great news.
-[dog panting]

156
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:46,570
-Yuru.
-Uh?

157
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:48,150
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
Thank you for coming.

158
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,280
The heck did I do?

159
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:52,450
You should save your thanks
for Asa.

160
00:08:52,530 --> 00:08:54,620
Yeah. I'll thank her, too.

161
00:08:55,830 --> 00:08:59,210
I was just so happy to see
you actually came. [sniffles]

162
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:00,370
[Yuru grunts softly]

163
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:03,210
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Thanks, Yuru.
And sorry.

164
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,880
I won't lie to you anymore.
[cries]

165
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,170
[Yuru grunts softly]

166
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:10,510
[YURU] Hmm.

167
00:09:10,590 --> 00:09:11,720
♪

168
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:19,310
[Danji (Tsugai) shouting]
And Asa... Thank you, too!

169
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:23,270
Huh? Whoa, hey, back off!
I didn't do it for you!

170
00:09:23,350 --> 00:09:25,520
I'm only here 'cause
I wanted to save Yuru!

171
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:28,440
Plus, this mission supported
the Kagemoris!

172
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:31,860
In fact, I hope Higashi Village
gets wiped off the map!

173
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:33,780
You and your sister
are a lot alike.

174
00:09:33,870 --> 00:09:35,370
What? How so?

175
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:37,530
The violent maniac part?

176
00:09:37,950 --> 00:09:40,080
Hey, Big Daddy Kagemori!

177
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:42,920
You'll find Shingo
at the TT Logistics office!

178
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,500
We're a little busy here.

179
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:46,130
Mind taking care of him?

180
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:48,050
Oh, can do.

181
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:51,050
Let's go. We're not done.

182
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:52,260
[BOTH] Sir.

183
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,890
Hey, Yuru!
I'll see you soon, 'kay?

184
00:09:57,510 --> 00:09:58,720
Later.

185
00:09:58,810 --> 00:10:00,640
[exclaims]

186
00:10:00,730 --> 00:10:01,890
[cries]

187
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:05,230
[ASA] Such a casual response
for his little sister! [cries]

188
00:10:05,310 --> 00:10:08,150
And hey! He actually agreed
we'd meet up later!

189
00:10:08,230 --> 00:10:12,150
-Very moving.
-I'm so happy I can't walk.

190
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,650
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
By the way, Yuru,

191
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:15,370
you mentioned something
about Left and Right

192
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:17,870
having a lead on your parents.
What's that about?

193
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:18,950
Oh, yeah.

194
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,580
I guess you wouldn't know
they went missing

195
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,120
after they came down
the mountain.

196
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:24,160
But we might just have a clue.

197
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:26,250
Left and Right are in the middle
of fighting a guy

198
00:10:26,330 --> 00:10:28,460
who knows something.
I'd better head there.

199
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,000
-Idiot.
-Wait, what?

200
00:10:30,090 --> 00:10:32,340
Why wouldn't you go to them
before me?

201
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,130
Who do you think
you're calling an idiot?

202
00:10:34,220 --> 00:10:35,340
You just said they're missing.

203
00:10:35,430 --> 00:10:37,390
That should always be
your top priority.

204
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,640
You've gotta value
your ma and pa!

205
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,390
And who says I don't?

206
00:10:41,470 --> 00:10:42,640
Look, emotions are high,

207
00:10:42,930 --> 00:10:44,730
and I could really do
without being called an idiot.

208
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:47,440
You know your precious
Asa-In-A-Cell was a phony.

209
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,900
And I'd been playing you
for a fool all these years, too!

210
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:52,740
So of course I'd call you
an idiot for choosing us!

211
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,070
You are!

212
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:56,660
Ah! You guys
did string me along.

213
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,870
Thanks for reminding me
of that, you big jerk!

214
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,030
-You're an idiot.
-[YURU] Shut up, idiot!

215
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,580
[FEMALE DAEMON]
Seems like they made up.

216
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:03,160
-[MALE DAEMON] Seems so.
-[YURU] I'm not an idiot.

217
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:04,750
You're an idiot, idiot!

218
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:07,750
[GUARD] More to do?

219
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:12,050
Aw, man.
I just think I need a vacation.

220
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:14,090
This job is exhausting.

221
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:16,930
[brakes squeak]

222
00:11:24,730 --> 00:11:26,020
[GUARD] Come on.

223
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:27,940
It's out of batteries?

224
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,320
HQ told me
they restocked everything.

225
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:31,360
[groans]

226
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:33,780
And someone really bothered

227
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:36,610
busting one of these
old warehouses open. Great.

228
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:39,370
The thieves must have used
some heavy-duty stuff.

229
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:41,620
Hmm?

230
00:11:42,370 --> 00:11:43,370
[sighs]

231
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:46,080
How annoying.

232
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,210
[lever clunks]

233
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:49,790
♪

234
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:54,340
[guard trembling]

235
00:11:57,470 --> 00:11:58,430
[thuds]

236
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,680
[panting]

237
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,640
Who do we call? An ambulance?

238
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:05,680
No way. The police! HQ! HQ!

239
00:12:05,770 --> 00:12:07,890
Something terrible's
happened here!

240
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:13,270
[running footsteps]

241
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:19,610
This is a rifle, Yuru.

242
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,700
It's the long-range weapon
you saw me use

243
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:23,580
in our fight
against Tenaga-Ashinaga.

244
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,870
A single shot from this baby
could very well be lethal.

245
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,750
If I plug an ordinary person
with it,

246
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:32,340
the shock alone might kill them
even if I miss their vitals.

247
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:34,880
Just keep in mind
that if I do have to use this,

248
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,800
I can't guarantee the unlucky
recipient will survive.

249
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:39,090
[YURU] Mm-hmm.

250
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:41,640
[DERA] Since we're after info
on your folks,

251
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,350
I'd like to capture the pervert
and his daemons alive.

252
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:45,720
This guy's skilled enough

253
00:12:45,810 --> 00:12:47,680
to take one of Left's arms off,
though.

254
00:12:47,770 --> 00:12:50,060
I'll do my best,
but it's a tall order.

255
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:51,690
Left lost one of her arms?

256
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,440
The old girl honestly
took it surprisingly well.

257
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:55,770
But it just goes to show you

258
00:12:55,860 --> 00:12:58,240
this guy and his katana daemons
are bad news.

259
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,240
No matter what happens,

260
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,570
I want you
to keep your distance.

261
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:02,490
-[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Oh.
-Even I'm not confident

262
00:13:02,570 --> 00:13:03,950
I could dance toe-to-toe
with him,

263
00:13:04,030 --> 00:13:05,620
so I'll be supporting you
from afar

264
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:06,830
with my little friend here.

265
00:13:07,330 --> 00:13:08,370
I understand.

266
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,960
-[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Yuru.
-[YURU] Huh?

267
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,500
I can sense Left and Right.
This way.

268
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:15,880
[both grunt]

269
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,170
-[loud crash]
-[BOTH] Hm?

270
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,220
[YURU] Yeah, that's them.

271
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,630
[DERA] They're still fighting.

272
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:25,510
Sorry in advance
if we can't take the perv alive.

273
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:27,890
But risking your life
isn't an option.

274
00:13:27,970 --> 00:13:30,140
If things start to go south,
I'm gonna shoot.

275
00:13:30,230 --> 00:13:33,020
That said,
I'll also be ready to fire

276
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:34,730
if you give me the signal.

277
00:13:34,810 --> 00:13:36,570
-Sound good?
-Hm.

278
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:40,450
[Right grunting]

279
00:13:46,830 --> 00:13:47,870
[Right gasps]

280
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:52,210
[chuckles]

281
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:54,710
Was the whole spiel
about trying to take me alive

282
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:56,380
some kind of joke, or what?

283
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,380
That thing would've killed me!

284
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,010
Don't fret, lad!

285
00:14:00,090 --> 00:14:02,760
I wasn't aiming
with the intent to hit you.

286
00:14:06,350 --> 00:14:08,720
I can't speak for Left, though.

287
00:14:09,770 --> 00:14:11,520
♪

288
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:27,080
Yuru!

289
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,540
[IVAN] The moon!

290
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:35,380
Damn it. He's backlit!

291
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,880
[grunting]

292
00:14:47,850 --> 00:14:50,310
Hey, Left and Right,
I'm sorry if I hit you.

293
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:54,140
[LEFT] It matters not!
Loose your arrows!

294
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:58,900
They pose us no threat.

295
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:11,580
[Right laughs]

296
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:17,630
[YURU]
Hey, over here! Uh... pervert!

297
00:15:17,710 --> 00:15:20,250
Seriously, where did this
accusation come from?

298
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:23,170
Daemon katana man! Let's talk!

299
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:25,380
I hear you have info
on my parents!

300
00:15:26,010 --> 00:15:27,760
I don't like wasting arrows.

301
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,350
Surrender, and you can tell us
what you know.

302
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:33,180
I don't remember your parents
off the top of my head.

303
00:15:33,270 --> 00:15:36,310
Maybe it would jog my memory
if you came down here.

304
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:38,190
Nice try there,
but I'm good here.

305
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,270
Figured. [scoffs]

306
00:15:41,570 --> 00:15:42,440
Huh.

307
00:15:43,530 --> 00:15:45,570
The kid's raining death
from above,

308
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:48,240
and Left and Right
have got my flanks.

309
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,740
What's worse,
they can keep fighting

310
00:15:50,830 --> 00:15:53,240
after any injury
without a care in the world.

311
00:15:53,330 --> 00:15:55,330
What a pain to deal with!

312
00:15:55,410 --> 00:15:58,790
You were the one who attacked
Higashi Village, weren't you?

313
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,790
We've rescued the hostages,
and your buddy Shingo's

314
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:04,170
getting destroyed by
the Kagemori Clan as we speak.

315
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:07,050
What? The old man
hired all those soldiers

316
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,680
and still got beat?

317
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:11,970
I no longer have any reason
to negotiate with you guys.

318
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,350
You know about my parents.

319
00:16:14,430 --> 00:16:15,980
Now, tell me everything.

320
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:18,310
Or don't, and die.

321
00:16:19,310 --> 00:16:22,820
I see. I guess it's curtains
for Mr. Shingo.

322
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:25,820
Well then, it's not like
I've got any obligation

323
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:28,240
to keep serving
some washed-up nobody,

324
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,070
so I'll spill the beans.

325
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:34,330
Of course,
not like Shingo matters here.

326
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:37,210
He didn't have a thing
to do with your parents.

327
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:40,370
I was the one who killed
Mine and Nagisa.

328
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:41,670
[Yuru gasps]

329
00:16:44,210 --> 00:16:45,750
Cut off their heads.

330
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,920
[Right grunts]

331
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:51,380
Now, I should prepare a gift
for my next client.

332
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:52,800
[Right growls]

333
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,310
[Left gasps]

334
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:01,270
Yuru needs to get Seal,

335
00:17:01,350 --> 00:17:03,150
and we want it
to go nice and smooth.

336
00:17:03,730 --> 00:17:05,610
Meaning, you gotta die, Left.

337
00:17:07,570 --> 00:17:08,860
[Ivan grunts]

338
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:10,450
♪

339
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,630
[YURU] Which arm did you use
to cut down my parents?

340
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:37,010
The next shot I fire
goes into that one.

341
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,180
[GONZO] That so?

342
00:17:40,730 --> 00:17:42,640
Well, good work, everyone.

343
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:44,400
Make sure he stays restrained

344
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,190
until I can get back
to the manor.

345
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,030
[Gonzo sighs]

346
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:52,780
They said Akio betrayed us,
just as we feared.

347
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:54,240
[Fuyuki sighs]

348
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:56,030
[Gonzo grunts]

349
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:58,990
Let's clean up this mess
so we can hurry home.

350
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:04,000
[wind blowing]

351
00:18:05,540 --> 00:18:08,050
[DERA]
He decapitated Mine and Nagisa?

352
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:09,340
Really?

353
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,510
They'd be more useful
as hostages than corpses,

354
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:14,220
so why kill them?

355
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,010
Wait.

356
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,430
Is he lying to get a rise
out of Yuru?

357
00:18:22,430 --> 00:18:25,650
Now... which arm
did I use again?

358
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,730
Mostly I just remember
their screams.

359
00:18:28,730 --> 00:18:29,860
[Ivan chuckles]

360
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:32,440
[Yuru breathes shakily]

361
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:44,540
[MINE] Take a deep breath in
and let it out slow.

362
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:47,210
That's it. Release your breath,

363
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:50,590
and with it, all the noise
inside of your mind.

364
00:18:50,670 --> 00:18:53,340
Stay calm and assess
your surroundings.

365
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:55,340
Think about what you need to do.

366
00:18:55,630 --> 00:18:58,720
Consider what tools you have
on hand, in the moment.

367
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:01,140
That's how you'll survive.

368
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:04,520
I think I killed Mine
with my right arm

369
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,390
and Nagisa with my left.

370
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:09,150
Though, that might be backwards.

371
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,820
Take the bait, Yuru.

372
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:14,780
[Yuru continues
breathing shakily]

373
00:19:17,870 --> 00:19:22,160
Remember, death strikes where
our fears make us vulnerable.

374
00:19:22,950 --> 00:19:24,410
[Yuru grunting]

375
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:30,130
[IVAN] Waste your arrows.

376
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:33,420
What's wrong? The man
who killed your parents

377
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:36,760
is right in front of you.
Don't you wanna avenge them?

378
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:38,590
-[Yuru grunts]
-Give me an opening.

379
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,640
[YURU] I can't do it, Dad.

380
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:47,140
[Yuru breathing heavily]

381
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:50,860
[DERA] Keep your cool, Yuru.
Stay calm.

382
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:52,480
[Yuru grunting]

383
00:19:56,610 --> 00:19:59,450
[YURU] I can't silence the noise
in my mind.

384
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:05,160
They are alive and healthy,
I'm positive.

385
00:20:05,660 --> 00:20:07,500
[Yuru breathing shakily]

386
00:20:13,710 --> 00:20:16,460
[exhales and inhales deeply]

387
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,550
[exhales deeply]

388
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:27,180
[YURU] I won't believe it
till I've seen it.

389
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:28,390
[Ivan grunts]

390
00:20:28,890 --> 00:20:31,310
Put the demon katana
on the ground.

391
00:20:32,230 --> 00:20:34,150
[scoffs] Boring.

392
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:37,240
Would you have me hold on
to this one?

393
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:40,870
Wow, not even that's enough
to hurt you? Good grief.

394
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:43,280
You've got a guy behind me too,

395
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:46,330
and we've established running
isn't the best option.

396
00:20:47,370 --> 00:20:48,790
Pretty rough for me.

397
00:20:48,870 --> 00:20:50,540
I came here to play the cat,

398
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:53,090
but somehow I wound up
as the mouse.

399
00:20:53,630 --> 00:20:55,300
Well, this sucks.

400
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:57,170
I really hate
having to use this,

401
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:59,050
but you leave me no choice,

402
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:00,550
Daikyo?

403
00:21:02,430 --> 00:21:04,180
[Yuru and Dera gasp]

404
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:06,140
-[squelching]
-[LEFT] Hm?

405
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:07,970
♪

406
00:21:12,770 --> 00:21:15,520
Quick, Left,
lose that blasted thing!

407
00:21:15,610 --> 00:21:18,070
-[Left grunts]
-[Shokyo yelps]

408
00:21:19,110 --> 00:21:20,900
[Right grunts, yells]

409
00:21:22,910 --> 00:21:24,580
[Right yells]

410
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:28,200
[grunts]

411
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:32,540
[Danji (Tsugai) screams]

412
00:21:37,590 --> 00:21:39,880
-[LEFT] Right.
-What's wrong?

413
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,630
-He has done something bad.
-[RIGHT] Huh?

414
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,390
Get out of my way, Right!

415
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:47,560
I told you,
Lady Left's head is mine!

416
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,720
[RIGHT] Huh?

417
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:53,690
[Ivan grunts]

418
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

419
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:30,530
[ASUMA] That wasn't
terribly nice of you.

420
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:32,200
-[DERA] Yuru!
-[ASA] Brother.

421
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:34,620
[SHINGO]
Your demons control people?

422
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:36,920
I ain't about to let 'em
hijack my body.
